===CONTENT===

{#detect}
@summary: First-response detection and role assignment
# Detect and Declare

- Confirm the alert is real and customer-impacting.
- Assign incident commander and scribe.
- Open status channel and incident ticket.

Continue with {@mitigate} after declaration.
{/detect}

{#mitigate}
@summary: Short-term mitigation and risk reduction plan
# Mitigation Plan

Apply traffic shaping, feature flags, or service isolation.
If mitigation fails, execute {@rollback}.
Coordinate external comms through {@comms}.
{/mitigate}

{#rollback}
@summary: Controlled rollback sequence and verification checks
# Rollback

1. Freeze deployments.
2. Roll back to previous stable version.
3. Verify core endpoints and queue drain.
4. Update timeline in {@postmortem} notes.
{/rollback}

{#comms}
@summary: Internal and external communication checkpoints
# Communications

- Publish updates every 15 minutes.
- Include impact scope, mitigation status, and ETA.
- After recovery, link final notes to {@postmortem}.
{/comms}

{#postmortem}
@summary: Structured post-incident writeup and action tracking
# Postmortem

Capture timeline, root cause, blast radius, and follow-up actions.
Reference {@rollback} outcomes and communication quality from {@comms}.
{/postmortem}
